WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.535
An observation mission should begin with a specific question.

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:07.375
Examples include documenting construction progress, assessing storm damage,

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:09.160
confirming whether a route is obstructed,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.380
or recording the condition of an authorized asset.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.825
The question determines the scene, detail, timing, and collection method.

00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:16.640
Define the area of interest precisely.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.795
A smaller bounded area reduces flight time, data volume, and privacy impact.

00:00:20.795 --> 00:00:25.210
Identify boundaries that should not be crossed or recorded, including nearby homes,

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:28.190
sensitive facilities, people, or unrelated operations.

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.830
Specify required detail.

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.560
A broad overview may show access routes and terrain,

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.275
while an inspection may require closer authorized views.

00:00:35.275 --> 00:00:39.395
More detail is not automatically better; it increases storage, processing,

00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:42.240
and the chance of capturing unnecessary sensitive information.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.970
Choose the relevant time window.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.980
Lighting, traffic, weather, vegetation, tides, work schedules,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.350
and temporary obstructions can change what is visible.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.245
The observation should occur when it can answer the question safely and without creating

00:00:53.245 --> 00:00:54.240
avoidable impact.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.800
Record environmental constraints and decision criteria.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.668
State what would make the data usable, what conditions would require rescheduling,

00:01:00.668 --> 00:01:03.030
and which uncertainties the imagery cannot resolve.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:06.965
Avoid redesigning the mission in flight without a renewed risk and privacy review.

00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:08.925
Also define what should not be collected.

00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:12.840
Purpose limitation protects people and improves analysis by reducing noise.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:16.360
A clear objective creates a defensible link between the mission, each image,

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.440
and the final report.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:19.730
A useful objective also names the decision.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:22.915
If the audience must choose whether to send a ground inspection team,

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:26.520
the imagery should support that choice instead of producing a general scenic survey.
